  "query_preview": "..The main story this week will be the passage of\nmultiple shortwaves interacting with monsoon moisture that remains\nacross the state. The first will arrive this afternoon as an \nupper level Low traveling along the northern Tier trails a wave\nacross the state. Expect thunderstorm coverage to increase today\nwith individual storm motion moving off to the northeast. The\nhighest POPs favor the western zones today, with the best POPs\nmoving into the eastern zones on Monday as the wave pushes east. \n\nStarting on Tuesday a trough deepens off the West Coast. Another\nwave off this trough approaches Tuesday night through Wednesday \nmorning. This will be followed by another wave Thursday into\nFriday. Each of these waves will keep the daily shower and\nthunderstorm chances going. This last wave moving out on Saturday\nmorning may potentially bring some drier air into the area which\ncould confine precipitation chances to the far eastern part of the\nstate or push the precipitation all the way into the New Mexico\nbut we'll have to keep monitoring to see if that's the case.",
